# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. With CRLF the shebang line reads as
# "bash\r", so the kernel looks for an interpreter of that name and the script
# refuses to run at all on Linux/macOS:
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# That happened twice to the deploy_batocera.sh scripts after merges, so pin it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never line-ending-convert or diff these as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Note: much of quantum-pong/ is still committed with CRLF (sources, README,
# pyproject...). That's untidy but harmless -- Python and the tooling read it
# fine -- so it's deliberately left alone rather than renormalised here, which
# would rewrite ~25 files in one go and collide with anything in flight. To do
# it later, add `* text=auto eol=lf` above and run `git add --renormalize .`
# as its own separate commit.
